<div class="cookie-gate" id="cookie-gate" role="dialog" aria-modal="false"
     aria-labelledby="cookie-title" aria-describedby="cookie-text" hidden>
  <div class="cookie-inner">
    <p class="kicker" id="cookie-title">A word before you go further</p>
    <p class="cookie-text" id="cookie-text">This site keeps nothing on your machine unless you let it.
    There are <strong>no advertising cookies, no trackers and no third-party analytics</strong> here — we
    sell nothing and measure no one. What we would like to store is small and local: your sign-in, so the
    oracle knows you on your return, and what you have asked it, so a conversation survives a reload.
    <a href="/join/">What an account is for</a>.</p>
    <div class="cookie-actions">
      <button class="btn" type="button" id="cookie-yes">Accept</button>
      <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="cookie-no">Decline</button>
    </div>
    <p class="muted xsmall">Decline and everything still works — the site simply forgets you between
    visits, and you will be asked for your code each time. You can change your mind from the foot of any
    page.</p>
  </div>
</div>
